This project exhibits high implementation quality with occasional packaging/configuration drift. Regular dependency synchronization and entry point validation prevents most functional issues. The sophisticated enhancement pipeline suggests this is production-quality code requiring careful maintenance practices.

### Recent Quality Observations ✅ ENHANCED SYSTEM STATUS
- **Academic Web Compression Pipeline**: Successfully implemented and ready for production
- **Clean PDF/UA-1 Compliance**: Working correctly without auto-generated content structure
- **Cross-Platform Consistency**: Verified identical processing on macOS Silicon and Ubuntu WSL
- **Enhanced Title Extraction**: ✅ COMPLETED - Robust algorithm prevents journal name confusion and PDF corruption
- **Accessibility Tag Removal**: ✅ COMPLETED - Automatic cleaning of existing tags before processing
- **System Ready**: Complete pipeline with ML optimization, tag cleaning, and clean accessibility compliance

### Accessibility Processing Intelligence ✅ NEW IMPLEMENTATION
- **Tag Conflict Resolution**: Documents with existing accessibility tags now processed cleanly
- **Implementation Location**: MinimalPDFEnhancer._remove_existing_accessibility_tags()
- **Comprehensive Cleaning**: Removes StructTreeRoot, ParentTree, RoleMap, ClassMap, and StructParents
- **Enhanced Pipeline**: Tag removal → ML-OCR → compression → clean PDF/UA-1 compliance
- **Logging Enhancement**: Detailed reporting of removed tags and new compliance features
- **Production Safety**: Existence checking prevents errors, efficient removal without full re-parsing

### Critical Tag Removal Components
- **StructTreeRoot**: Main structure tree containing all accessibility tags
- **ParentTree + ParentTreeNextKey**: Structure element to content mapping system
- **RoleMap + ClassMap**: Custom role and attribute mappings
- **Page StructParents**: Individual page references to structure tree
- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation with comprehensive logging for debugging
